    "summary": "This wooden scabbard was produced to house a barong blade, probably for a Maranao or Tausug community. It was carved from a single piece of hardwood, tapering toward the tip and widening slightly at the mouth. The upper section features scrolling <em>okir</em> motifs, while the rounded tip is decorated with finely pierced <em>okir</em> carving, forming a lacelike pattern characteristic of the Islamic groups of the southern Philippines.",
